{"study_accession":"PRJNA839749","secondary_study_accession":"SRP377615","title":"Altered somatic hypermutation patterns in covid-19 patients predicts disease severity","description":"Much of the battle between the human body and SARS-CoV-2 relies on lymphocytes and their antigen receptors. Identifying and characterizing successful receptors is of utmost clinical importance. We report here the application of a machine learning approach utilizing B Cell Receptor (BCR) and T cell Receptor (TCR) repertoire sequencing data taken from severe and mild SARS-CoV-2 infected individuals and uninfected controls. In contrast to previous studies, our approach was successful in stratifying non-infected from infected individuals, as well as disease level of severity. The features that drive this classification can be used to build and adapt therapeutic strategies to covid-19, and constitute a proof of concept for future epidemiological challenges.","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":28,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN28552913","study_accession":"PRJNA839749","blood_class":"whole_blood","class_from":"sample","title":"Human sample from Homo sapiens","description":"Human sample from Homo sapiens","sex":"not applicable","geo_sample":"","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2023-04-03","attributes":[["isolate","Cov_73_first-exp"],["age","not applicable"],["biomaterial_provider","Rabin"],["sex","not applicable"],["tissue","blood"],["disease","covid"],["disease_stage","case mild"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR19445417","experiment_accession":"SRX15498711","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"RANDOM","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":57948927,"base_count":5215403430,"first_public":"2023-04-03","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: BCR sequence of adult humans"}],"labels":[]},{"sample_accession":"SAMN28552915","study_accession":"PRJNA839749","blood_class":"whole_blood","class_from":"sample","title":"Human sample from